  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Passing chain – beat the lap",
  "description": "Two teams. The blue team spread out inside a coned square with one ball. Each player has a letter (or number) and they pass in order: A to B, B to C and so on, then the chain starts again. The red team line up by a corner outside the square and dribble a lap round the square, one at a time.\n\nBlue count their passes while red run their relay. Then swap jobs – which team made more passes? Variation: race the clock – can you get the ball all the way round the chain in 20 seconds? The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Know who you pass to – look up before the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass with the inside of the foot for accuracy."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Take your first touch towards where you're passing next."
    }
  ],
